Strain gauges, full-field measurements and model validation (@mech-strain-measurement: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY", #source "../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W", #mechanical-engineering "../computation/Finite-elements-from-virtual-work-to-an-assembled-model.lingua#r_7T1F6870T0VKQAGE9QWFC2TA29") { r_5GX4N1Q7XDQ9DPVWVJWSGR9N36
**Read:** [Modules in Mechanics of Materials — David Roylance](../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY), Experimental Solutions and Tensor Transformations; [Applied Mechanics of Solids — Allan F. Bower](../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W), constitutive laws and boundary conditions. Carry forward the metrology distinction between the measurement model and the mechanical model.

A strain gauge averages deformation over a finite grid in a particular direction and bonding condition. Its electrical response needs a calibrated conversion and compensation for influences such as temperature and lead resistance. A rosette combines several directional strains to infer in-plane components; infer stress only after stating a constitutive law and plane-stress or plane-strain assumption.

For a 0°/45°/90° rosette in small strain, ε_x = ε_0, ε_y = ε_90 and γ_xy = 2ε_45 − ε_0 − ε_90. Readings 500, 400 and −100 microstrain give γ_xy = 400 microstrain. This is engineering shear, twice the tensor component.

Digital image correlation follows image texture to estimate displacement and strain over an observation surface. Calibration, perspective, subset size, filtering, lighting and spatial differentiation influence the result. A visually dense field is not automatically an accurate local strain at a crack tip.

**Work:** Predict directional strains from a known tensor, synthesize rosette readings and recover the original components. Then assess a real or documented measurement with uncertainty, gauge placement and constitutive assumptions. Compare a global displacement and local strain from the same loading; disagreement can reveal an incorrect boundary or load path that either observation alone misses.

